    "publishedAt": "2026-11-05",
    "summary": "During the fiscal second quarter, which Nintendo defines as the period between July and September instead of the traditional Q3, the company shipped 2.67 million Nintendo Switch 2 consoles. This marks a decrease of 41% from 4.54 million units a year earlier and a 30% decline from 3.82 million units in the April-June quarter. Switch 2 software sales rose 26% to 15.03 million units, led by new releases like Splatoon Raiders, which achieved 2.42 million sales, and Fire Emblem: Fortune's Weave, with 1.34 million sales. The original Switch software reached 31.92 million units, bolstered by Rhythm Heaven Groove, which sold 2.89 million units.",
