    "summary": "The infographic below provides the key highlights for the quarter: Here are what the results mean and how they were achieved: Total revenue for Arm in Q2 FYE27 increased 27% year over year to $1.44 billion, representing Arm's highest ever second quarter. Record second quarter was driven by strong licensing and other revenue of $773 million, reflecting a 50% year-over-year increase, an important leading indicator of future royalty growth. Meanwhile, royalty revenue for the quarter reached $670 million, with data center royalties doubling year over year. For the first time, Arm's partners reported more than 10 billion Arm-based chips shipped during the quarter - an increase of 1.5 billion chips year over year - adding to the scale of the platform already used by more than 30 million developers.",
